###  https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#StructureFamily
battgpt:StructureFamily rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf emmo:EMMO_b7bcff25_ffc3_474e_9ab5_01b1664bd4ba ;
                        rdfs:comment "Structural-prototype classification of a crystal structure (e.g. which well-known battery-material structure type it belongs to: layered oxide, olivine, spinel, garnet, sulfide superionic conductor, ...). New in v0.3.0. Confirmed absent from EMMO core, EMMO domain-battery, EMMO domain-electrochemistry, EMMO domain-chemical-substance, and EMMO's work-in-progress domain-crystallography ontology (v0.1.0, not imported here) — this branch is a genuine BattGPT extension, not a restatement of an upstream concept. It is deliberately the deepest local subclass hierarchy in the ontology: it is the intended conditioning vocabulary for hyperbolic (OnT) embedding and for CrystaLLM soft-prompt conditioning. A composite concept like 'Layered Oxide Cathode' is not given its own class; it is queried as a material with hasStructureFamily some LayeredOxideStructure and belongsToElectrode PositiveElectrodeRoleIndividual, which avoids a combinatorial explosion of family-x-role classes, most of which would never be populated."@en ;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#> ;
                        rdfs:label "StructureFamily"@en ;
                        skos:definition "Structural-prototype classification of a crystal structure."@en ;
                        skos:prefLabel "StructureFamily"@en .


